model_response:
O problema é que você está tentando completar o GeckoResult com um PromptResponse, mas o GeckoResult está esperando um GeckoResult<PromptResponse>. Além disso, você está tentando usar métodos que não existem no GeckoResult.

Aqui está uma versão corrigida do seu código:

```java
@Override
public GeckoResult<PromptResponse> onFilePrompt(GeckoSession session, FilePrompt prompt) {
    // Your existing code to start the file chooser intent
    Intent intent = new Intent(Intent.ACTION_GET_CONTENT);
    intent.setType("*/*");
    intent.addCategory(Intent.CATEGORY_OPENABLE);
    currentFilePrompt = prompt;
    filePromptFuture = new CompletableFuture<>();

    // Assume "this" is an Activity or Fragment
    startActivityForResult(intent, FILE_UPLOAD_REQUEST_CODE);

    // Create a new GeckoResult
    GeckoResult<PromptResponse> geckoResult = new GeckoResult<>();

    // When the CompletableFuture is completed, complete the GeckoResult
    filePromptFuture.whenComplete((geckoResult0, throwable) -> {
        if (throwable != null) {
            geckoResult0.completeExceptionally(throwable);
        } else {
            geckoResult0.thenAccept(result -> {
                GeckoResult<PromptResponse> newGeckoResult = new GeckoResult<>();
                newGeckoResult.complete(result);
                geckoResult = newGeckoResult;
            });
        }
    });

    return geckoResult;
}
```

Nesse código, estamos criando um novo GeckoResult e completando-o com o resultado obtido do CompletableFuture. Em seguida, estamos substituindo o GeckoResult original com o novo GeckoResult. Isso permite que o GeckoResult seja completado com um PromptResponse.

To force a `TextField` in Adobe XD to display columns in JavaScript, you can use the following code:

```javascript
const textField = document.querySelector('text-field');

if (textField) {
  const width = textField.offsetWidth;
  const height = textField.offsetHeight;

  // Calculate the number of columns
  const columns = Math.ceil(Math.sqrt(width / 200)); // assuming 200px per column

  // Set the number of columns
  textField.style.gridTemplateColumns = `repeat(${columns}, 200px)`;

  // Set the grid template rows
  textField.style.gridTemplateRows = 'repeat(auto-fit, minmax(50px, 1fr))';
}
```

This code calculates the number of columns based on the width and height of the `TextField`. It assumes 200px per column, but you can adjust this value as needed.

The `gridTemplateColumns` property is set to `repeat(${columns}, 200px)`, which creates a grid with the specified number of columns, each with a width of 200px.

The `gridTemplateRows` property is set to `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(50px, 1fr))`, which creates a grid with a dynamic number of rows that automatically adjusts to fit the content.

Note that this code should be run after the `TextField` has been rendered, so it's recommended to run it in a function that is called after the component has been created.

Also, note that this is just a basic example, and you may need to adjust the values and the CSS properties to fit your specific use case.

Here's a complete example:

```javascript
const textField = document.querySelector('text-field');

if (textField) {
  const width = textField.offsetWidth;
  const height = textField.offsetHeight;

  // Calculate the number of columns
  const columns = Math.ceil(Math.sqrt(width / 200)); // assuming 200px per column

  // Set the number of columns
